{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Tunics of skin.</b> Some say that at first there was bone and flesh, and now He covered them with skin. Others say: tunics for their skin. Yet others say that there is a beast in the likeness of a human, and HaShem commanded and its skin was flayed. We have no business investigating this; we need only believe that HaShem made for the human and for his wife tunics of skin. Who can recount His mighty deeds, who can tell His works and wonders — there is no searching His greatness:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:03.708072346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}